module nywd-criminal-local-rules.local-rules

import core.authority.{ CaseOrder }
import core.frcrimp45.{ frcrimp45 }

// The Western District of New York's own criminal periods, counted under
// the criminal rules (FRCrimP 45(a) governs "any local rule"). Unless the
// assigned District Judge orders otherwise, the motion procedures apply to
// indictments and informations (Loc. R. Crim. P. 12). No trigger carries a
// service method: FRCrimP 45(c)'s three added days follow the manner of
// service, which is not modeled here.
//
// Periods that are FRCrimP periods stay in lit/frcrimp: objections to a
// magistrate judge's order or recommended disposition follow FRCrimP 59
// (Loc. R. Crim. P. 59(c)).
//
// Conditions that are not deadlines from an event stay in notes: at or
// after arraignment the court issues an order setting discovery and motion
// deadlines (Loc. R. Crim. P. 12(a); not vendored); a letter application
// to exceed a page limit is made at least seven days before the date the
// memorandum must be filed (Loc. R. Crim. P. 12(c)), a period counted back
// from another deadline; an edited video deposition is delivered at least
// three days before it is shown and objections to it are served at least
// 24 hours before (Loc. R. Crim. P. 15(f)), periods from a showing the
// court schedules during trial; and a search warrant matter not timely
// returned is unsealed 28 days from the warrant's issuance, or at the
// return if earlier, unless the court orders it kept sealed (Loc. R. Crim.
// P. 41(c), (d)), a step of the court rather than of a party.
//
// The earlier W.D.N.Y. criminal outline's FRCrimP flow and its decisions
// (United States v. Salerno, Barker v. Wingo, Zedner v. United States,
// Brady v. Maryland and the others it named) are FRCrimP, Speedy Trial
// Act or constitutional authority and belong to lit/frcrimp; they are
// removed here: no reporter text is vendored.

/// A memorandum in support of or in opposition to a motion: at most 25
/// pages (W.D.N.Y. Loc. R. Crim. P. 12(c)).
limit motion-memorandum {
  pages <= 25 cite "W.D.N.Y. Loc. R. Crim. P. 12(c)"
} cite "W.D.N.Y. Loc. R. Crim. P. 12(c)"

/// A reply memorandum: at most 10 pages; no sur-reply without the judge's
/// permission (W.D.N.Y. Loc. R. Crim. P. 12(c), (d)).
limit reply-memorandum {
  pages <= 10 cite "W.D.N.Y. Loc. R. Crim. P. 12(c)"
} cite "W.D.N.Y. Loc. R. Crim. P. 12(c)"

/// A motion is served (W.D.N.Y. Loc. R. Crim. P. 12(b)).
event MotionServed() paper motion-memorandum
/// The responding papers are served (W.D.N.Y. Loc. R. Crim. P. 12(b)).
event ResponseServed() paper motion-memorandum
/// Reply papers are filed and served (W.D.N.Y. Loc. R. Crim. P. 12(b)).
event ReplyServed() paper reply-memorandum
/// The trial date (W.D.N.Y. Loc. R. Crim. P. 15(d)).
event TrialScheduled()
/// A party receives the Clerk's notice to remove its paper or other
/// physical exhibits (W.D.N.Y. Loc. R. Crim. P. 26(c)).
event ExhibitRemovalNoticed()
/// A search warrant is executed, or the time for its execution expires
/// (W.D.N.Y. Loc. R. Crim. P. 41(b)).
event SearchWarrantExecuted()
/// A party is served with a magistrate judge's recommended disposition
/// (W.D.N.Y. Loc. R. Crim. P. 59(c)(2)).
event RecommendedDispositionServed()

/// W.D.N.Y. Loc. R. Crim. P. 12(b)(2): if the Court sets no deadlines by
/// order (12(b)(1)), the opposing party has 14 days after service of the
/// motion to file and serve responding papers.
deadline opposition-period: 14.days after MotionServed() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "W.D.N.Y. Loc. R. Crim. P. 12(b)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// W.D.N.Y. Loc. R. Crim. P. 12(b)(2): absent a court order, the moving
/// party has 7 days after service of the responding papers to file and
/// serve reply papers.
deadline reply-period: 7.days after ResponseServed() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "W.D.N.Y. Loc. R. Crim. P. 12(b)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// W.D.N.Y. Loc. R. Crim. P. 15(d): unresolved objections made at a
/// deposition recorded on video and stenographically are submitted by a
/// motion in limine no later than seven days before trial or any earlier
/// deadline the Court sets.
deadline video-deposition-objections: 7.days before TrialScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "W.D.N.Y. Loc. R. Crim. P. 15(d)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// W.D.N.Y. Loc. R. Crim. P. 26(c): a party that does not remove its paper
/// or other physical exhibits within 30 days from the date of the Clerk's
/// notice may have them destroyed or otherwise disposed of.
deadline exhibit-removal: 30.days after ExhibitRemovalNoticed() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "W.D.N.Y. Loc. R. Crim. P. 26(c)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// W.D.N.Y. Loc. R. Crim. P. 41(b): an executed search warrant is returned
/// with its inventory to the designated Magistrate Judge within 14 days
/// after it is executed or the time for execution has expired.
deadline search-warrant-return: 14.days after SearchWarrantExecuted() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "W.D.N.Y. Loc. R. Crim. P. 41(b)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// W.D.N.Y. Loc. R. Crim. P. 59(c)(2): a party seeking more time to object
/// to a magistrate judge's recommended disposition moves the District
/// Judge for an extension within 14 days after being served with it.
deadline objection-extension-motion: 14.days after RecommendedDispositionServed() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "W.D.N.Y. Loc. R. Crim. P. 59(c)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}
